@@ -72,6 +72,25 @@ EE.on('another-event', emitted, context);
 EE.removeListener('another-event', emitted, context);
 ```
 
+### Subscriptions
+
+`EventEmitter.subscribe` adds a persistent listener like `on`, but returns an
+idempotent function for cancelling that exact registration. Calling the
+cancellation function does not affect other registrations of the same listener,
+and it is safe to call after `off`, `removeListener` or
+`removeAllListeners`.
+
+```js
+var unsubscribe = EE.subscribe('event-name', emitted, context);
+
+unsubscribe();
+unsubscribe(); // no-op
+```
+
+Unlike `off` (an alias of `removeListener`), which removes all matching
+listeners for an event, a subscription cancellation only removes the
+registration that created it.
+
 ### Tests and benchmarks
 
 To run tests run `npm test`. To run the benchmarks run `npm run benchmark`.
